# Keystone :: topic authorisation
#
# %u is the connecting client's username, and use_identity_as_username makes that the
# certificate CN - the device id assigned by the CA. A device therefore cannot read or
# write another device's topics even with a perfectly valid certificate.
#
# Authentication answers "who are you"; this file answers "what may you touch". A PKI
# without an ACL gives every enrolled device the run of the broker.

pattern readwrite devices/%u/#
pattern read fleet/announcements

# The control plane connects with its own certificate and needs the whole tree.
user keystone-control-plane
topic readwrite #
